bodyHtml: |
  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Shaded by reed screens, on the bends of the Treizain road, La Moune beach is the only "real" developed beach in the town of Gassin — partly private and dedicated to a sailing school (courses, private lessons, equipment rental), with a relaxed, sporty atmosphere. It lies on the Treizain road, on the Gulf of Saint-Tropez side.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Gassin tourist office (gassin.eu) and Visit Var list "animals accepted" for La Moune beach. They specify neither a leash requirement nor a possible ban period, and we have not read a municipal bylaw: keep your dog on a leash and follow the signs. Note: the beach does not appear in the list of dog-friendly beaches of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez published by Grimaud Tourisme, which does cite Le Treizain. Access is free, 1 April to 31 October every day (Visit Var).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: this is not a spot for sporty swimming far out, as the sailing school trainees sail right in front — stay close to the shore with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p><a href="/en/fiche-plage-treizain-gassin">Le Treizain beach</a> is right next door, on the same road. The hilltop village of Gassin, ranked among the "Plus Beaux Villages de France", is a few minutes away by car.</p>
    </div>

